{"id":"ce63e07f-7f66-424d-a08a-a9c78e5104d2","object":"chat.completion","created":1784885351,"model":"deepseek-v4-flash","choices":[{"index":0,"message":{"role":"assistant","content":"{\n  \"implementation\": \"def solve(case):\\n    lines = case.get(\\\"lines\\\", [])\\n    trajectory = []\\n    error_line = None\\n    for idx, line in enumerate(lines):\\n        # expected format: \\\"Type: content\\\"\\n        # type can be any non-empty string before the first \\\": \\\"\\n        if \\\": \\\" in line:\\n            colon_index = line.index(\\\": \\\")\\n            typ = line[:colon_index]\\n            content = line[colon_index+2:]\\n            trajectory.append({\\\"type\\\": typ, \\\"content\\\": content})\\n        else:\\n            error_line = idx\\n            break\\n    valid = error_line is None\\n    return {\\n        \\\"valid\\\": valid,\\n        \\\"error_line\\\": error_line,\\n        \\\"trajectory\\\": trajectory\\n    }\"\n}","reasoning_content":"We need to create the solve function for AGENT-RA-01 based on the provided description. The task is likely about parsing a trajectory from lines. The input case has \"lines\" array. The output should have \"trajectory\" array of objects with \"content\" and \"type\". Also \"valid\" boolean and \"error_line\" null or integer. \n\nThe lines seem to be of various types: Thought, Action, Observation, Final. Possibly other types? The task is to parse them into a trajectory. The output schema requires trajectory items with type and content. The lines may have a prefix like \"Thought: \" and then content. So we need to split each line by \": \" (colon space) to get type and content. Check if the line matches that pattern, otherwise set error_line to the line index? Also valid if all lines are well-formed? Or maybe the task is to validate the trajectory format. Given the examples, the lines all have proper prefix. But the task might be to handle invalid lines. The error_line should be null if no error, else the 0-based index of the first erroneous line? Or maybe the line number? The schema says \"integer\" for error_line. So likely the index of the first line that doesn't match expected pattern, or zero-based.\n\nAlso note that the trajectory should include all lines? The examples show 5 lines. The output might be to convert each line into an object. The final type \"Final\" might be allowed? In the schema, \"type\" is string, no restriction. So we can use the prefix as type. So algorithm: iterate over lines, try to split at first \": \" (colon space). If the line has a colon space, type is the part before, content is the part after. If not, set error_line to index (0-based) and return with valid=False. If all lines are well-formed, set valid=True and error_line=null. Return the trajectory as list of objects.\n\nCheck the case: lines are exactly that pattern. So for these cases, valid=true, error_line=null, trajectory = [{\"content\":\"inspect\",\"type\":\"Thought\"},{\"content\":\"lookup\",\"type\":\"Action\"},{\"content\":\"found\",\"type\":\"Observation\"},{\"content\":\"answer\",\"type\":\"Thought\"},{\"content\":\"done\",\"type\":\"Final\"}]\n\nBut the spec says \"return one JSON object with exactly one key, `implementation`\". So we need to output a JSON string containing the Python source. The source should define solve(case) that returns a dict with keys \"valid\", \"error_line\", \"trajectory\". Must be standard library only.\n\nAlso note: The case argument is the payload object directly. So case is a dict with \"lines\" and \"_case_nonce\". Use case[\"lines\"].\n\nImplement carefully.\n\nEdge cases: Line could have colon but no space? The pattern is \": \" (colon space). If there is colon without space, it's invalid. Also if no colon at all, invalid. Also if line is empty? Then no colon, invalid. So handle.\n\nReturn type: JSON-serializable dict.\n\nWrite code. Return as JSON string with escaping.\n\nNow produce the final answer."},"logprobs":null,"finish_reason":"stop"}],"usage":{"prompt_tokens":917,"completion_tokens":848,"total_tokens":1765,"prompt_tokens_details":{"cached_tokens":0},"completion_tokens_details":{"reasoning_tokens":661},"prompt_cache_hit_tokens":0,"prompt_cache_miss_tokens":917},"system_fingerprint":"fp_8b330d02d0_prod0820_fp8_kvcache_20260402"}